  artifacts/references/stage3_literature_reading_record.md:18:| Joly (2012), elementary PML introduction | PDF pp. 6--7, 9--11, 14--17, 19--20 | PML is characterized by impedance matching/zero reflection; construction via complex coordinate change \(x\mapsto x+(i\omega)^{-1}\int\sigma\); in 2D only the derivative in the PML direction is stretched; adding isotropic damping to all components is not generally perfectly matched. | Defines the planar-interface/stretched-coordinate test used in the v2 mismatch proof. |
  artifacts/references/stage3_literature_reading_record.md:19:| Baffet--Grote--Imperiale--Kachanovska (2019) | PDF pp. 4--11 and 35 | For the second-order wave PML, a non-naive augmented energy with shifted variables and time integrals decays for constant damping; variable/piecewise damping introduces gradient/interface remainders, so monotone decay is not automatic. | Provides the model for what a genuine dissipative PML energy must contain and justifies constant-coefficient scope for sharp identities. |
  artifacts/references/stage3_literature_reading_record.md:20:| Bécache--Fliss--Kachanovska--Kazakova (2021) | PDF pp. 2--8 | Classical Cartesian PML for Maxwell can become unstable in some anisotropic 3D diagonal media; stability is model-dependent and tied to backward waves/group velocity. | Used as a caution that perfect matching and stability are distinct properties. |
  artifacts/references/stage3_literature_reading_record.md:21:| Bécache--Kachanovska--Wess (2023) | PDF pp. 4--10 and references pp. 39--40 | For dispersive waveguides, the PML is derived in the Laplace domain after eliminating polarization; the stretch uses \(1+\sigma/(s\zeta(s))\). Material passivity/admissibility and the choice of \(\zeta\) matter for stability; the paper gives a time-domain auxiliary-variable PML and exponential truncation error theorem. | Supports using the physical material law \(A(s)\) in the stretched-coordinate derivation, rather than replacing it by \(A(s+\rho)\). |
  artifacts/references/stage3_literature_reading_record.md:22:| Huang--Li--Liu (2023) | PDF pp. 1--6 | Equivalent Berenger PML models have nontrivial stability analysis; an explicit unconditionally stable finite-element scheme is built for an equivalent model, while variable-damping energy stability remains difficult. | Used to classify equivalent Berenger/ADE systems as plausible but not automatically monotone in the simple \(L^2\) energy. |
  artifacts/references/stage3_literature_reading_record.md:23:| Meza-Fajardo--Papageorgiou (2008), local `A_Nonconvolutional...pdf` | PDF pp. 1--6, 8--10, 19, 23, 26 | M-PML adds damping in multiple coordinate directions; stability can improve, but it is a modified absorbing layer with parameters chosen for spectral stability. | Used for the MPML repair option and for the statement that stabilizing modifications can sacrifice exact perfect matching. |
  artifacts/references/stage3_literature_reading_record.md:24:| Correia--Jin (2006) | PDF pp. 1--5 | Regular PML, CFS-PML, and second-order PML have different absorption strengths; CFS helps evanescent waves but can hurt low-frequency propagating waves, while higher-order PML combines mechanisms. | Used for the CFS/ADE candidate classification, not as an energy proof. |
  artifacts/references/stage3_literature_reading_record.md:25:| Feng--Li (2013) | PDF pp. 1--4 and 6--9 | Higher-order stretched-coordinate PML can be implemented through ADE variables and can improve late-time/evanescent absorption in computations. | Used to justify an ADE time-domain realization of rational stretch factors. |
  artifacts/references/stage3_literature_reading_record.md:27:| Xie--Zheng--Cristini--Zhang (2023) | PDF pp. 1--7 and 13 | M-PML is explicitly described as losing perfect matching because of multiaxial stretching, though frequency shifting improves near-grazing and long-time behavior. | Used to state that MPML-type repairs should be labeled stable/absorbing, not perfectly matched. |
  artifacts/references/stage3_literature_reading_record.md:28:| `references/main.pdf` | PDF pp. 4--6, 38--40, 42--48, 54--56 | Local manuscript derives UPML/Cole--Cole frequency-domain forms, 2D energy boundedness, stretched-coordinate PML notes, and CFS-PML attempts; formulas are partly unreadable in extraction. | Used as local project context; no independent formula claim is taken from unreadable displays. |
